#AUTO 10
#NEEDED 0
# Device health check — the "is anything broken?" smoke test.
#
# Brings up each controller and verifies it answers with its
# known-good signature, then dumps the key state registers. Run
# this whenever the device misbehaves and compare the log against a
# known-good capture; a changed value points straight at the
# subsystem that drifted.
#
# Load read-only (no --writes flag). The only state changes are the
# CALL bring-ups, which are the normal boot steps anyway.
#
# !!! SAFETY: reading a peripheral whose clock is GATED hangs the
# bus (this is the exact failure the eMMC bring-up hit). This script
# only touches blocks that are clocked at probe time: the CRU and
# GRF families are always on; SD and USB are brought up by
# kernel_main before the probe runs; the eMMC is read only after
# CALL emmc_init ungates it. It deliberately does NOT read the
# display or audio controllers — their clocks are off. To probe one
# of those, ungate its clock first (a W to the right CLKGATE_CON,
# needs --writes) and only then read it.

LOG ===== CLOCKS: main CRU gate registers CLKGATE_CON0..19 =====
LOG (eMMC=CON9 0x324, USB3=CON10 0x328, SDMMC0=CON15 0x33C)
DUMP 0xFDD20300 20

LOG ===== RESETS: main CRU SOFTRST_CON0..19 =====
DUMP 0xFDD20400 20

LOG ===== CCLK_EMMC source mux (CLKSEL_CON28 bits 14:12) =====
R 0xFDD20170

LOG ===== PMU CRU gate registers PMUGATE_CON0..2 =====
DUMP 0xFDD00180 3

LOG ===== GRF: eMMC pin mux (GPIO1B_H, GPIO1C_L, GPIO1C_H) =====
DUMP 0xFDC6000C 3

LOG ===== SD card controller (DW MSHC @ 0xFE2B0000) =====
LOG HCON hardware-config + STATUS (SD is up from kernel_main)
R 0xFE2B0070
R 0xFE2B0048

LOG ===== USB2 PHY GRF (@ 0xFDCA0000) =====
LOG CON0 should be 0x0C52 (OTG port normal, not suspended)
EXPECT 0xFDCA0000 0x00000C52 0x0000FFFF
DUMP 0xFDCA0000 4

LOG ===== eMMC: bring up and verify signature =====
CALL emmc_init
LOG SDHCI capabilities should read 0x226DC881 on this board
EXPECT 0xFE310040 0x226DC881 0xFFFFFFFF
LOG read block 0: rc 0 with a real (non-FFFFFFFF) word0 = healthy
CALL emmc_read0

LOG ===== health check complete =====
